A SESSION'S KNOB POSITIONS, SHOWN AS IT OPENS — the CLAP wrapper of clap-juce-extensions. Applied by
cmake/PatchedWrappers.cmake to the pinned commit (ORBITAMP_CLAP_EXT_TAG, 51a9359) to every CLAP this tree
builds, an amp's own and the family's alike; git apply reads from the first "diff --git" line on, so this
text is not part of the patch.

The wrapper's state load hands the stream to setStateInformation and returns, and never tells the host the
parameters' values have changed. Through the processor's parameter listeners each new value does reach the
host, but as an output event on its next process or flush — which a host may take for automation — and a
host that looks right after the load still sees the values of before: clap-validator's three
state-reproducibility tests fail with "After reloading the state, these parameter values changed without a
rescan request". CLAP asks a plug-in that loads a state to call clap_host_params.rescan with
CLAP_PARAM_RESCAN_VALUES (params.h, "Loading a preset"), and both calls are main-thread; so the load does,
where the host has the params extension. Not in the pinned commit nor upstream after it: the same change is
proposed there as free-audio/clap-juce-extensions#193, open.

diff --git a/src/wrapper/clap-juce-wrapper.cpp b/src/wrapper/clap-juce-wrapper.cpp
index 0b60b73..0edbcda 100644
--- a/src/wrapper/clap-juce-wrapper.cpp
+++ b/src/wrapper/clap-juce-wrapper.cpp
@@ -2443,6 +2443,10 @@ class ClapJuceWrapper : public clap::helpers::Plugin<
         // So we just have to assume it works.
         processor->setStateInformation(chunkMemory.getData(), (int)chunkMemory.getSize());
         chunkMemory.reset();
+        // A load reaches the host only as output events on its next flush; CLAP asks for a values
+        // rescan instead (params.h, "Loading a preset"). load and rescan are both main-thread.
+        if (_host.canUseParams())
+            _host.paramsRescan(CLAP_PARAM_RESCAN_VALUES);
         return true;
     }
 
